Anyway, I frequently use this as a part of my bag of tricks to gain
experience early in the game.  Once I have more experience points I
am less likely to use such risky techniques.

Another good one if you have levitation and telepathy, or levitation and
a blindfold (or just plain a blindfold, if you are brave - actually I've
done it with no special devices, but then I enjoy tempting death ;^) )
is to find a magic trap and spend some time stepping into it.

The 2 things you want to protect yourself against are blindness and being
surrounded and beaten to death.  Use telepathy or a blindfold against the
former, and use a writing tool and levitation to protect against the latter.

I get bored during the first 10 exp levels or so (I've seen them so many
times), so I use risky behavior to get past them quickly.  After that there
are other ways to gain experience...
